tools.description:
Cancel an advanced order (e.g. an OCO) by order_id, cancelling all of its legs. Resolve order_id via get_advanced_orders; pass the same account_number. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__cancel_advanced_order(args: {
  // Brokerage account that owns the advanced order. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true. The upstream rejects mismatches against the order's owning account.
  account_number: string;
  // Advanced-order UUID from get_advanced_orders. Must live in account_number.
  order_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Advanced-order UUID the cancel was requested for.
  order_id: string;
  // 'pending_cancel' — the broker accepted the cancel request (asynchronous; not yet cancelled) — or 'cancelled'.
  request_status: string;
};
  // request_status 'pending_cancel' means the broker accepted the cancel request (asynchronous) — NOT that the order is already cancelled. For the final state, call get_advanced_orders. On error the cancel was rejected outright — report verbatim.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Cancel an open equity order by order_id. Always confirm with the user before calling. Resolve order_id via get_equity_orders if the user refers to it by symbol or description; pass the same account_number. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call. Cancellation may be rejected if the order has already filled, was already cancelled, or is otherwise ineligible.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__cancel_equity_order(args: {
  // Brokerage account that owns the order. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true. The upstream rejects mismatches against the order's owning account.
  account_number: string;
  // Order UUID from get_equity_orders. Must live in account_number.
  order_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // True when the broker accepted the cancel request.
  accepted: boolean;
};
  // accepted=true means the broker accepted the cancel request, NOT that the order is already cancelled (cancellation is asynchronous). For the final state, call get_equity_orders: state 'pending_cancelled' = in flight; 'cancelled' or 'partially_filled_rest_cancelled' = succeeded; any filled state = a fill raced the cancel. Offer to check the final state. On error, the cancel was rejected outright — report verbatim.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Fetch advanced orders (OCO — one-cancels-the-other — and other multi-leg contingency orders) for an account, each with its legs' underlying equity orders hydrated. Call this alongside get_equity_orders when you want to get a full picture of the user’s orders.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__get_advanced_orders(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts.
  account_number: string;
  // Filter by kind: 'oco', 'oto', or 'fx_at_trade'.
  contingency_type?: string;
  // Lower bound (inclusive). ISO 8601 UTC or YYYY-MM-DD; naive values are interpreted as UTC.
  created_at_gte?: string;
  // Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; for the next page, pass the prior response's next value back verbatim.
  cursor?: string;
  // Filter to a single advanced order by its UUID (the id from a prior result).
  order_id?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Advanced orders on this page, each with its legs. Empty when the account has none matching the filters.
  advanced_orders: null | Array<null | {
  // Brokerage account number that owns this advanced order.
  account_number: string;
  // The sub-order legs of this advanced order. For an OCO: two equity legs — a take-profit limit and a stop-loss. Each link references its underlying equity order by order_id.
  advanced_order_links: null | Array<{
  // Whether this leg is the primary sub-order. OCO legs have no primary.
  is_primary?: null | boolean;
  // Hydrated underlying equity order for this leg (symbol, side, type, prices, state, fills) — same shape as get_equity_orders orders[]. Populated by get_advanced_orders; absent on create/review responses and when the leg could not be fetched.
  order?: null | {
  // True when the order originated from an agent's request, regardless of who submitted it: either an agent submitted it directly (Trade Approvals off), or the customer reviewed an agent's proposal and approved it in the Robinhood app (Trade Approvals on). Identifies agent-initiated orders in general, not orders initiated by this agent specifically. False when the customer created the order in the app with no agent involved.
  agent_initiated: boolean;
  // Weighted average fill price across executions. Null until the first fill.
  average_price: null | string;
  // When the order was created.
  created_at: string;
  // Shares filled so far. Less than quantity while partially filled; equal once filled.
  cumulative_quantity: string;
  // Notional amount for dollar-based market orders; null for share-quantity orders.
  dollar_based_amount: null | {
  // Quoted-decimal amount, e.g. '100.00'.
  amount: string;
  // ISO currency code; always 'USD' for equity orders today.
  currency_code: string;
};
  // Per-fill detail; reference only for per-lot questions.
  executions: null | Array<{
  // Per-execution fees (regulatory + clearing) in USD.
  fees: string;
  // Execution UUID.
  id: string;
  // Fill price per share.
  price: string;
  // Shares filled in this execution.
  quantity: string;
  // When the fill occurred.
  timestamp: string;
}>;
  // Cumulative fees (regulatory + clearing) in USD.
  fees: string;
  // Order UUID; needed by cancel_equity_order.
  id: string;
  // Instrument UUID; resolve to symbol via the instruments endpoint if needed.
  instrument_id: string;
  // Time of the most recent fill, cancel, or reject. Null on a brand-new unfilled order.
  last_transaction_at: null | string;
  // 'regular_hours', 'extended_hours', or 'all_day_hours'.
  market_hours: string;
  // Source that finally submitted or approved the order: 'user' (app), 'agentic' (MCP), 'recurring', 'drip', or other internal system values. An agent-proposed order the customer approved in the app reads 'user' here; use agent_initiated to recognize it as agent-initiated.
  placed_agent: string;
  // Limit price for limit/stop_limit orders; null for market orders.
  price: null | string;
  // Originally-requested share quantity. Null for dollar-based orders before the first fill.
  quantity: null | string;
  // Idempotency key the order is stored under, unique per account. Usually the ref_id passed to place_equity_order; an order placed through a trade approval carries that approval's id instead. Omitted when the order has none.
  ref_id?: string;
  // Free-text reason when state is 'rejected'.
  reject_reason?: string;
  // 'buy' or 'sell'.
  side: string;
  // Lifecycle state: new, queued, unconfirmed, partially_filled, filled, cancelled, rejected, failed, voided, pending_cancelled, partially_filled_rest_cancelled, and (for short-sale orders) locating, locate_failed.
  state: string;
  // Stop trigger price for stop_market/stop_limit orders; null otherwise.
  stop_price: null | string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // 'gfd' (good for day) or 'gtc' (good till cancelled).
  time_in_force: string;
  // 'immediate' (market/limit) or 'stop' (stop_market/stop_limit).
  trigger: string;
  // Upstream type: 'market' or 'limit'. Combine with trigger to recover the user-facing market/limit/stop_market/stop_limit.
  type: string;
};
  // UUID of the underlying equity order for this leg. Null for a non-equity leg. Look up full leg detail via get_equity_orders when order is not hydrated.
  order_id: null | string;
}>;
  // Whether auto-send was enabled at placement time.
  auto_send_enabled: boolean;
  // Advanced-order kind: 'oco' (one-cancels-the-other — filling either leg cancels the other), 'oto', or 'fx_at_trade'.
  contingency_type: string;
  // When the advanced order was created.
  created_at: string;
  // Advanced-order UUID (the root advanced order). Pass to cancel_advanced_order.
  id: string;
  // When true, a partial fill on one leg proportionally reduces the sibling leg rather than leaving it at full size.
  proportional_triggering: boolean;
  // Client idempotency key echoed back from placement.
  ref_id: string;
  // Lifecycle state of the advanced order as a whole: 'unconfirmed' (not yet confirmed by the venue), 'confirmed', 'queued', 'partially_filled', 'filled', 'pending_cancelled', 'cancelled', 'rejected', 'failed', 'voided'.
  state: string;
  // When the advanced order was last updated (equals created_at until the first update).
  updated_at: string;
}>;
  // Opaque cursor for the next page — NOT a URL. When non-empty more pages exist: call this tool again with cursor set to this value verbatim, leaving the other arguments unchanged. Empty on the last page.
  next?: string;
};
  // Each entry is a contingency group; advanced_order_links are its legs. For an OCO the two legs are a take-profit limit and a stop-loss — filling either cancels the other. When a link's order is present, read leg detail (symbol, prices, state, fills) from it; when only order_id is present, fetch it via get_equity_orders. Describe the group by its state plus its legs. If next is non-empty, more pages exist — call again with cursor set to that value verbatim.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Read whether trades on an account currently require the customer's manual approval before they execute. Call this before telling the customer whether approvals are on or off, and before any step whose workflow depends on the answer. Takes account_number (from get_accounts). Only the customer can change this setting, in the Robinhood app; no tool here turns it on or off. To instead list the approvals waiting on the customer, use get_trade_approvals.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__get_trade_approval_setting(args: {
  // Alphanumeric brokerage account number to read the trade-approval setting for — the account_number field from get_accounts, NOT the numeric rhs_account_number. Must be an account accessible to this agent. Only agentic accounts have this setting; non-agentic accounts are rejected. Required.
  account_number: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // The account's current trade-approval setting.
  setting: {
  // The account this setting applies to. Echoes the account_number that was passed in.
  account_number: string;
  // Whether trades on this account currently require the customer's manual approval before they execute. When false, most agent-placed trades execute immediately, but an individual trade can still require approval under a policy that applies regardless of this setting — so do not promise that no trade will need approval.
  human_must_approve_trades: boolean;
  // RFC3339 timestamp of when the setting was last changed. Present it as 'as of <time>' when telling the user the current state; may be empty if the upstream did not return it.
  updated_at?: string;
};
};
  // This is the state as of this call — the customer can change the setting in the Robinhood app at any time, so read it again before a later statement about it rather than reusing this one. When human_must_approve_trades is already true and the customer asks to turn approvals on, tell them approvals are already on. Changing this setting in either direction is the customer's to do in the Robinhood app, so when they want it changed, point them there instead of offering to do it. A FORBIDDEN error means the account is not accessible to this agent (or not the user's), and a 4xx error means the account_number is missing or invalid or the account is not agentic — surface that rather than retrying, and reconfirm the account_number from get_accounts.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

List the pending trade approvals waiting on the customer for an account — orders the agent placed that require the customer's manual approval before they execute. Call this every time before stating what is or is not pending: the customer approves and declines in the Robinhood app and pending approvals expire on their own, so an earlier result — or anything said earlier in the conversation — may already be wrong. Takes account_number (from get_accounts); optionally filter by asset class. To instead check the current state of specific approvals (in any state), pass their ids in approval_ids.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__get_trade_approvals(args: {
  // Alphanumeric brokerage account number to list pending trade approvals for — the account_number field from get_accounts, NOT the numeric rhs_account_number. Must be an account accessible to this agent. Required.
  account_number: string;
  // Optional list of specific approval ids to fetch, all in this account, at most 100 per call. When set, the tool returns exactly these approvals in any state (pending, approved, declined, expired, or auto-approved) instead of listing pending ones, and asset_class/cursor are ignored. Ids not in this account are omitted from the result.
  approval_ids?: null | Array<string>;
  // Optional filter to one asset class. One of ASSET_CLASS_EQUITY, ASSET_CLASS_OPTION, ASSET_CLASS_CRYPTO. Omit for all classes. Ignored when approval_ids is set.
  asset_class?: string;
  // Pagination cursor. Omit for the first page; to fetch the next page, pass the value from the prior response's next field. Ignored when approval_ids is set.
  cursor?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Place an OCO (one-cancels-the-other) equity order with real money: a take-profit limit leg and a stop-loss leg on the same symbol, side, and quantity, where filling one cancels the other. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

When review_advanced_order came back with customer_approval_required true and no alert, call this tool straight away with no confirmation step in the conversation, because this call does not place the order: it goes to the customer to approve or decline in the Robinhood app. Otherwise, including whenever an alert is present, follow review_advanced_order's own guide.

Idempotency: pass a fresh UUID as ref_id on the first call and re-send the same ref_id on transient retries.

OCO rules:
- Both legs use the same symbol, side, and quantity.
- take_profit_limit_price and stop_loss_stop_price are required and must differ.
- For a sell OCO (protecting a long): take_profit_limit_price must be ABOVE stop_loss_stop_price. For a buy OCO (covering a short): stop_loss_stop_price must be ABOVE take_profit_limit_price.
- time_in_force can be GFD or GTC. market_hours must be regular_hours (the only session OCO supports) — omit it or pass regular_hours explicitly.
- take_profit_limit_price and stop_loss_stop_price must each be at least 0.25% away from the current market price, and at least $0.10 apart from each other, or the order will be rejected — don't propose prices tighter than that.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__place_advanced_order(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true; non-agentic accounts are rejected.
  account_number: string;
  // 'regular_hours' — the only session OCO supports; extended_hours and all_day_hours are rejected. Both legs share it.
  market_hours?: string;
  // Whole-share quantity. Both legs use the same quantity.
  quantity: string;
  // Idempotency key (UUID) for the advanced order. Generate once per logical order and re-send on transient retries; a fresh key is generated when omitted.
  ref_id?: string;
  // 'buy' or 'sell'. Both legs use this side (an exit for an existing position: 'sell' to protect a long, 'buy' to cover a short).
  side: string;
  // Stop trigger price of the stop-loss leg. The stop-loss leg is always a stop-market order — there is no stop-limit option for it.
  stop_loss_stop_price: string;
  // Stock symbol. Both OCO legs are on this symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Limit price of the take-profit leg.
  take_profit_limit_price: string;
  // Can be 'gfd' or 'gtc'. Both legs share it.
  time_in_force?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Place a real equity order with real money. Parameters mirror review_equity_order plus the optional ref_id. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

Workflow: by default call review_equity_order first. When it comes back with customer_approval_required true and no order_checks alert, call this tool straight away with no confirmation step in the conversation, because this call does not place the order: it goes to the customer to approve or decline in the Robinhood app. Otherwise, including whenever order_checks is non-empty, follow review_equity_order's own guide.

Idempotency: pass a fresh UUID as ref_id on the first call for each logical order, and re-send the SAME ref_id on retries of transient transport failures. Use a new ref_id only when the user wants a new order.

Parameter rules:
- If the user has not specified type, ask. For immediate fills with price protection, prefer a marketable limit at the current ask over a plain market.
- Outside regular hours, only limit orders execute. For an immediate fill during extended or overnight/24-hour sessions, place a limit order (a marketable limit at the current ask) with market_hours set to that session — not a market order. Market and stop orders are regular_hours-only; placed after hours as regular_hours they queue for the next regular open.
- Provide exactly one of quantity or dollar_amount, and take the value from the user — if they did not say how much, ask. Never substitute a default such as 1 share or $100. dollar_amount requires type=market (server computes shares from last_trade_price).
- Fractional shares: only on type=market with market_hours=regular_hours, eligible accounts, up to 6 decimal places, no short sells.
- limit_price required for limit/stop_limit; stop_price required for stop_market/stop_limit.
- Fractional and dollar-based orders only place in regular_hours; the tool rejects them in other sessions.
- tax_lots (specified-lot selling, sell only): to sell specific lots, first call get_equity_tax_lots for the symbol, then pass tax_lots as {open_lot_id, quantity} pairs whose quantities sum to the order quantity. Omit for default (FIFO) cost basis. US accounts only; not allowed with dollar_amount, stop orders, all_day_hours, or fractional limit orders.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__place_equity_order(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true; non-agentic accounts are rejected.
  account_number: string;
  // USD notional (e.g. '100.00'). Only valid with type=market.
  dollar_amount?: string;
  // Limit price; required for limit or stop_limit.
  limit_price?: string;
  // 'regular_hours' (default, 9:30–16:00 ET), 'extended_hours' (pre-/post-market), or 'all_day_hours' (the 24 Hour Market / overnight session). extended_hours and all_day_hours execute limit orders only — market, stop_market, and stop_limit are regular_hours-only and are rejected if tagged to another session.
  market_hours?: string;
  // Number of shares. Decimals (fractional) allowed for market + regular_hours only.
  quantity?: string;
  // Idempotency key (UUID). Generate once per logical order and re-send on retry — the upstream deduplicates by ref_id. Omitting falls back to a server-generated key (loses client↔gateway idempotency).
  ref_id?: string;
  // 'buy' or 'sell'.
  side: string;
  // Stop trigger price; required for stop_market or stop_limit.
  stop_price?: string;
  // Stock symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Optional specified-lot selection for a SELL order. To sell specific tax lots instead of the default FIFO cost basis, pass the exact lots as {open_lot_id, quantity} objects, where open_lot_id comes from get_equity_tax_lots and the quantities sum to the order quantity. Omit for default FIFO. Sell only; at most 30 lots; US accounts only. Not allowed with dollar_amount, stop_market/stop_limit, all_day_hours, or fractional-share limit orders.
  tax_lots?: null | Array<{
  // open_lot_id of the open tax lot to sell, from get_equity_tax_lots.
  open_lot_id: string;
  // Shares to sell from this lot as a decimal string; at most the lot's quantity_available.
  quantity: string;
}>;
  // 'gfd' or 'gtc'. Default: gfd.
  time_in_force?: string;
  // 'market', 'limit', 'stop_market', or 'stop_limit'.
  type: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Simulate an OCO equity order without placing it; returns any pre-trade alert (buying power, instrument halt, etc.). Parameters mirror place_advanced_order. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

OCO rules:
- Both legs use the same symbol, side, and quantity.
- take_profit_limit_price and stop_loss_stop_price are required and must differ.
- For a sell OCO (protecting a long): take_profit_limit_price must be ABOVE stop_loss_stop_price. For a buy OCO (covering a short): stop_loss_stop_price must be ABOVE take_profit_limit_price.
- time_in_force can be GFD or GTC. market_hours must be regular_hours (the only session OCO supports) — omit it or pass regular_hours explicitly.
- take_profit_limit_price and stop_loss_stop_price must each be at least 0.25% away from the current market price, and at least $0.10 apart from each other, or the order will be rejected — don't propose prices tighter than that.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robinhood_trading__review_advanced_order(args: {
  // Brokerage account number. Must come from the user or be clearly implied — never default from get_accounts. Must be agentic_allowed=true; non-agentic accounts are rejected.
  account_number: string;
  // 'regular_hours' — the only session OCO supports; extended_hours and all_day_hours are rejected.
  market_hours?: string;
  // Whole-share quantity. Both legs use the same quantity.
  quantity: string;
  // 'buy' or 'sell'. Both legs use this side.
  side: string;
  // Stop trigger price of the stop-loss leg. The stop-loss leg is always a stop-market order — there is no stop-limit option for it.
  stop_loss_stop_price: string;
  // Stock symbol. Both OCO legs are on this symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Limit price of the take-profit leg.
  take_profit_limit_price: string;
  // Can be 'gfd' or 'gtc'.
  time_in_force?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Tool-specific result payload; see the inner properties for fields.
  data: {
  // Pre-trade alert. Absent/null means the checks passed with no warnings.
  alert?: null | {
  // Alert-specific detail payload (e.g. the exceeded limit). Shape varies by alert_type; present verbatim.
  alert_details?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // Lowercase alert name paralleling alert_type.
  alert_name: string;
  // Machine alert code in UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g. 'EQUITY_MAX_NOTIONAL_EXCEEDED'). New codes ship regularly — surface verbatim, do not enumerate.
  alert_type: string;
};
  // True when the customer must approve this order in the Robinhood app before it executes. False when it executes as soon as it is placed. Absent when it was not determined for this order.
  customer_approval_required?: null | boolean;
  // Which rule made approval necessary, so the reason can be given rather than asserted. 'account_setting' means the customer has trade approvals turned on for the account. 'mandatory_model' means the AI model handling this request requires approval for every trade, even with the account setting off. Absent when approval is not required.
  customer_approval_required_reason?: string;
  // Compliance market-data disclosure string (NBBO bid/ask with sizes + venue codes, last trade, and update time). Display this verbatim to the user. Empty only when live prices were unavailable.
  market_data_disclosure?: string;
  // Live market data (single quote) for the shared OCO leg symbol; same shape and semantics as get_equity_quotes results[0].quote.
  quote_data: null | {
  // Prior-day close adjusted for splits, dividends, and mergers.
  adjusted_previous_close: string;
  // Lowest current sell-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable.
  ask_price: string;
  // Highest current buy-order price. Zero when the book is closed or unavailable.
  bid_price: string;
  // False for instruments that have never traded; price fields are meaningless when false.
  has_traded: boolean;
  // Most recent pre-market / after-hours / overnight trade. Null during regular hours or when the symbol does not trade in the current session.
  last_non_reg_trade_price: null | string;
  // Most recent regular-hours trade (9:30-16:00 ET). Stays frozen at the closing print after the close until the next open; not the official settled close.
  last_trade_price: string;
  // Raw prior closing print — not corporate-action adjusted and not the official settled close.
  previous_close: string;
  // YYYY-MM-DD trading date that previous_close corresponds to. Null for symbols that have never had a settled close.
  previous_close_date: null | {};
  // Instrument listing state — 'active' is normal; other values (inactive, delisted, unlisted) mean the instrument is not in normal trading state.
  state: string;
  // Ticker symbol.
  symbol: string;
  // Timestamp of ask_price.
  venue_ask_time: string;
  // Timestamp of bid_price.
  venue_bid_time: string;
  // Timestamp of last_non_reg_trade_price. Reveals which non-regular session the trade came from.
  venue_last_non_reg_trade_time: null | string;
  // Timestamp of last_trade_price.
  venue_last_trade_time: string;
};
};
  // This tool does NOT place the order. When customer_approval_required is true and no alert is present, call place_advanced_order immediately with the same parameters, presenting nothing and asking for no confirmation: this call does not execute the order, the customer sees it in the Robinhood app and approves or declines it there, so confirming here asks for the same consent twice. Carry customer_approval_required_reason into what you tell the user once that call returns, so they hear why the order needs approving and not only that it does; give no cause when it is absent. A present alert cancels that: present and confirm exactly as below whatever customer_approval_required says, so a flagged order is never sent for approval without the user seeing the alert. When customer_approval_required is false or absent, present the plan (both legs with symbol, side, quantity, and prices) and get explicit confirmation before calling place_advanced_order, surfacing any alert verbatim; a null/absent alert means no broker warnings, NOT that confirmation can be skipped. Whenever you show the user a price or quote from this response you MUST also display market_data_disclosure exactly as provided, verbatim and unmodified, as the required compliance quote disclosure.
  guide: string;
}>>; };
```

Simulate a stock order without placing it. Returns the current quote plus pre-trade alerts (buying power, PDT, instrument halt, etc.). Call this by default before place_equity_order unless the user has very explicitly asked to skip review. Requires an agentic_allowed=true account; non-agentic accounts are rejected — do not call.

Parameter rules:
- If the user has not specified type, ask. For immediate fills with price protection, prefer a marketable limit at the current ask over a plain market.
- Outside regular hours, only limit orders execute. For an immediate fill during extended or overnight/24-hour sessions, place a limit order (a marketable limit at the current ask) with market_hours set to that session — not a market order. Market and stop orders are regular_hours-only; placed after hours as regular_hours they queue for the next regular open.
- Provide exactly one of quantity or dollar_amount, and take the value from the user — if they did not say how much, ask. Never substitute a default such as 1 share or $100. dollar_amount requires type=market (server computes shares from last_trade_price).
- Fractional shares: only on type=market with market_hours=regular_hours, eligible accounts, up to 6 decimal places, no short sells.
- limit_price required for limit/stop_limit; stop_price required for stop_market/stop_limit.
- Fractional and dollar-based orders only place in regular_hours; the tool rejects them in other sessions.
